<overview>
<p>Anti-BattleMech jump platoons combine the extreme danger of close-assault tactics against armored targets with jump pack mobility that allows approach from unexpected angles. Armed with assault rifles and explosive charges, these platoons use vertical movement to reach BattleMech upper torsos, cockpits, and sensor arrays that ground-based anti-BattleMech infantry cannot easily access. The jump capability improves approach options but does nothing to reduce the fundamental lethality of attacking a BattleMech at close range.</p><p>Equipped with laser rifles that offer superior range and armor penetration compared to ballistic weapons, these platoons field one of the most effective personal arms available to conventional infantry, though the weapons are significantly more expensive and require soldiers to carry additional power packs.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on prototype date for anti-Mek equipment
</notes>

